# Pinned MinIO mint image for the external SDK acceptance run in ci/mint/run.sh.
#
# WHY A DIGEST AND NOT A TAG
#   minio/mint is archived, and Docker Hub still carries two tags for it: `latest` (built
#   2024-05-28) and `edge` (built 2026-01-08). A tag can be re-pointed at any time; a digest
#   cannot. Two runs pulled from one digest ran the same SDK builds, and nothing else makes
#   two runs comparable.
#
# WHY THIS DIGEST
#   It is the `edge` build, the only one made from the archived repository's final tree.
#   Its manifest is single-platform linux/amd64. Mint publishes no arm64 build at all, so an
#   arm64 host runs it under emulation, and timings measured that way are not performance
#   evidence.
#
# HOW THIS PIN WAS RESOLVED (2026-09-12)
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect minio/mint:edge
#     -> MediaType application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json
#        Digest    sha256:08a05e68893c68be2a83b6f79556853ed6aa3c6c9e64c823a00853e4e55d2200
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect minio/mint:edge --format '{{json .Image}}'
#     -> "architecture": "amd64", "os": "linux", created 2026-01-08T10:41:21Z,
#        Entrypoint ["/mint/entrypoint.sh"], WorkingDir /mint
#   curl -s 'https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/minio/mint/tags?page_size=30'
#     -> exactly two tags, latest and edge, each a single amd64 image
#
# THE SDK CENSUS
#   MINT_SDKS names every directory under /mint/run/core in this image, hidden ones included.
#   When it is given no SDK names, mint's runner skips hidden directories, so `.minio-dotnet`
#   would never run. ci/mint/run.sh names every SDK explicitly, in this order, and refuses to
#   start when the image's own listing differs from this list:
#     docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 --entrypoint /bin/ls <MINT_IMAGE> -A /mint/run/core
#   Verified 2026-09-13 against the pulled image: exactly the 15 entries below. The same image's
#   /mint/mint.sh writes one log per SDK at /mint/log/<sdk>/log.json, which is what
#   ci/mint/report.py attributes records by.
#   ci/mint/baseline.txt must carry exactly one line per SDK here; see
#   scripts/check_mint_baseline.sh.
#
# HOW TO MOVE IT
#   Change the digest in its own pull request, re-run the workflow in `record` mode, and land
#   the resulting baseline separately. If one commit moves both the image and the tolerated
#   counts, nobody can tell an upstream change from a behaviour change.
#
# Sourced by ci/mint/run.sh.
MINT_IMAGE=docker.io/minio/mint@sha256:08a05e68893c68be2a83b6f79556853ed6aa3c6c9e64c823a00853e4e55d2200
MINT_PLATFORM=linux/amd64
MINT_SDKS=".minio-dotnet aws-sdk-go-v2 aws-sdk-java-v2 aws-sdk-php aws-sdk-ruby awscli healthcheck mc minio-go minio-java minio-js minio-py s3cmd s3select versioning"
